{
  "fixture": "panels-conditions",
  "extension": "panels-conditions",
  "about": "Highlight (UseHighlight) condition indicators: the opaque rectangle InDesign paints behind a conditioned range. Height = per line, above the baseline the largest (size x head.yMax of the face of each run) and below the largest (size x -head.yMin); see next/oracle/rules/condx-c4.ko.md. condx-hl-arial-12 and -times-12 were first measured by condx-c3 (artifacts/condx-c3-20261023/research); story: Alpha-bold-LARGE tail.<Br>Second paragraph here.<Br>Third line AV To office. The fonts new to the document (Georgia, Consolas, Verdana, Malgun Gothic) are measurement records in artifacts/condx-c4-20261023/research (appliedFont on a font the document lacks makes InDesign add Fonts.xml records and FontStyle=Regular overrides that Folio does not write yet). condx-hl-arial-24 and condx-hl-wrap are records too: the rectangles equal InDesign to 0.001 pt, but print-check shows a text-raster difference of 11.8 / 6.4 (limit 2.0) at 24 / 56 pt on the coloured rectangle.",
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "condx-hl-arial-12",
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "textFormat",
          "target": "format",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 70,
          "props": {
            "appliedFont": "Arial",
            "pointSize": 12
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "setConditionOptions",
          "name": "Print",
          "props": {
            "method": "USE_HIGHLIGHT"
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "setConditionIndicators",
          "mode": "SHOW_AND_PRINT_INDICATORS"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
